+
+## Maintained Dual permission bridge
+
+`--permission-replies` enables exact online asks for persisted JSON prompts only.
+An explicit finite `--timeout` and `--prompt-retries 0` are required; `exec` is
+unsupported. Existing automatic decisions remain unchanged. Only true asks emit
+`dual/permission/request` containing `requestKey`, `sessionId`, `promptId`,
+`ownerGeneration`, `rpcId`, `rawJson`, `rawSha256`, and `deadlineMs`.
+
+`permission-reply -s <name> --reply <json>` accepts that identity plus an offered
+once `optionId`, `commitRef`, and `commitSha256`. It sends one control request to
+the same live owner; it does not queue another prompt, recover an owner or retry.
+A `dual.native.permission.reply.v1` receipt with `consumed: true` confirms callback
+consumption, not tool execution or business acceptance. Unknown delivery must be
+reconciled externally. Restart, expiry, cancellation or mode/model/config changes
+cannot restore a callback. Host file/terminal confirmation uses the same exact
+lane, retaining existing path and permission-mode checks.
